      "message": "I believe that using the requested network here is not correct. For example, if a user requests a socket with a null network, they will receive three `onSocketCreated` callbacks. If the socket is then unrequested, `onSocketDestroyed` will be called three times with a null network. Instead, you should pass the network that is returned from onSocketCreated/onInterfaceDestroyed. For the onUnrequested case, I think you should store the network in mCallbackSockets.",
